  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.144pt, 445.03pt, "., the Fermi-level splitting and the external voltage at low to moderate forward bias are so ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 470.35pt, "completely decoupled that recombination can be both linear in external voltage and exponential in ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 495.67pt, "Fermi-level splitting at the same time. The requirement for this to happen are strong gradients of the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 520.99pt, "quasi-Fermi level at short circuit and moderate forward bias that will occur primarily in those layers that ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 546.19pt, "have low conductivities, that is in perovskite solar cells primarily the transport layers. As these apparent ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 571.54pt, "photoshunts will also occur in perovskite subcells used for tandem cells, it is important to investigate ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 596.86pt, "their effect on the overall tandem fill factor and efficiency. ")
  #line-at(84.984pt, 628.18pt, "While photoshunts have a somewhat complicated to explain origin, their mathematical description is ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 653.5pt, "conveniently ")
  #line-at(139.791pt, 653.5pt, "simple. ")
