  #line-at(70.824pt, 497.95pt, "To study how the current mismatch of individual sub-cells influences the tandem cell, we measured the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 516.91pt, "perovskite-Si tandem solar cell under a sun simulator containing a white LED and an infrared LED. The ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 535.87pt, "intensity of the 2 LEDs can be adjusted individually thus the tandem cell can be measured at different ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 554.83pt, "current not matching conditions. We kept the short circuit currents of tandem cells at a constant value ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 573.82pt, "while changing the intensities of white LED or IR LED. With the intensity of IR light irradiance ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 592.9pt, "increasing, the Si sub-cell generates an excess photocurrent not matched by the perovskite solar cell. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 611.86pt, "Thus, the photocurrent of the perovskite solar cell limits the overall photocurrent, thereby leading to an ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 630.82pt, "increased visibility of hysteresis features and the photoshunts in the tandem solar cell ")
